/code-review high — loop U4-late1, round 1, branch 2026-10-19-mobile-toolchain-tasks (main...HEAD = 6c2d56b)

[
  {"file": "tools/kotlin/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/kotlin", "line": 137, "summary": "The normal (check) run resolves with --write-locks, which rewrites the lock state from a fresh resolve. It does not validate against the committed lockfile, so any dynamic or range version moves to the newest release, and the check reports it as a lockfile the resolve changed.", "failure_scenario": "A module declares `com.foo:bar:1.+` with dependencyLocking, and its committed lockfile pins 1.2. Upstream publishes 1.3. Every developer's and CI's `mise run setup` then rewrites the lock to 1.3, puts the file under RESOLVED and exits 1 with 'Run setup:deps:kotlin --upgrade', even though nobody changed the build. The comment on line 76, 'Resolving fails on a mismatch with a lockfile', is also false under --write-locks."},
  {"file": "tools/android/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/android", "line": 102, "summary": "With no EMULATOR_IMAGE, the task needs a literal targetSdk and exits 1 without one. Android library modules (com.android.library) normally declare no targetSdk, because AGP 8 deprecated it for libraries.", "failure_scenario": "A repo holding only an Android library sets compileSdk = 35 and no targetSdk. `mise run setup` prints 'No targetSdk level found' and fails, even though the platform and tools could be installed. Every library repo has to set EMULATOR_IMAGE by hand before setup passes. Falling back to the compileSdk level would avoid this."},
  {"file": "tools/android/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/android", "line": 24, "summary": "AGP detection and detect_level only scan *.gradle.kts, build-logic/ and libs.versions.toml. Groovy build.gradle projects, and buildSrc convention plugins that pull AGP in as com.android.tools.build:gradle, are never detected, and the task exits 0 silently.", "failure_scenario": "Case 1: an Android app with app/build.gradle containing `id 'com.android.application'`. Case 2: modules apply a buildSrc convention plugin. In either case HAS_AGP stays false, the SDK platform, platform-tools and emulator image are never installed, and setup prints nothing. code:lint:android does handle build.gradle, so the two tasks disagree on what counts as an Android build."},
  {"file": "tools/android/.config/mise/tasks/code/lint/android", "line": 49, "summary": "module_of turns the nearest folder with a build file into a Gradle path (`:dir:sub`). The init script then calls `root.project(it)`, which throws for any folder that is not a project of this build at that path.", "failure_scenario": "A commit touches convention-plugins/src/main/kotlin/Foo.kt (an includeBuild other than build-logic/buildSrc), a samples/ folder excluded from settings, or a project with a custom projectDir. In each case BOOTSTRAP_LINT_MODULES contains an unknown path, Gradle fails with UnknownProjectException, and code:lint (and the pre-commit hook) blocks the commit."},
  {"file": "tools/swift/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/swift", "line": 39, "summary": "On a non-Darwin host the task prints a header and exits 1 instead of treating itself as not applicable. `setup` runs every setup:deps task in every environment, and the ci/prod/stage environments are Linux (os = \"linux\").", "failure_scenario": "A Swift package repo with the swift tool has CI that runs `mise run setup` on a Linux runner. setup:deps:swift prints 'Swift is macOS only' and fails the whole setup step, which blocks CI for a repo that may only need lint or format jobs there."},
  {"file": "tools/kotlin/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/kotlin", "line": 83, "summary": "The init script calls resolve() on every canBeResolved configuration of every project. In AGP and Kotlin Multiplatform builds, some resolvable configurations (legacy `default`/`archives`, KMP metadata and dependenciesMetadata configurations, internal AGP ones) fail variant selection or emit deprecated-resolution errors.", "failure_scenario": "An Android or KMP project with dependencyLocking runs `mise run setup`. bootstrapResolveAll hits an ambiguous-variant or not-meant-to-be-resolved configuration and fails, so setup fails for reasons unrelated to the lockfiles. The cleanup trap restores the files, but the developer cannot get past setup."},
  {"file": "tools/android/.config/mise/tasks/code/lint/android", "line": 27, "summary": "The lint gate exits 0 silently when ANDROID_HOME/platforms is missing, so a lint run on a machine or CI job where the SDK is not installed reports success without linting.", "failure_scenario": "On a fresh clone, or in a CI lint job that did not run setup:deps:android first, code:lint passes with no Android lint output. The user believes the commit was checked, while Android lint errors go through to main."},
  {"file": "tools/android/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/android", "line": 47, "summary": "detect_level takes the first hit in alphabetical file order, not the highest level across modules. Its regex also matches commented-out lines.", "failure_scenario": "A multi-module build has :aaa-legacy with compileSdk = 33 and :app with compileSdk = 35. The task installs platforms/android-33, which leaves the platform the build needs missing. Separately, a line `// compileSdk = 30` in an earlier file selects API 30."},
  {"file": "tools/kotlin/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/kotlin", "line": 43, "summary": "The lockfile paths come from `git ls-files` without -z, so non-ASCII paths are C-quoted (core.quotePath). The cp backup and the cmp/restore then work on names that do not exist.", "failure_scenario": "A module folder named `módulo/` makes git print `\"m\\303\\263dulo/gradle.lockfile\"`. `cp` at line 132 fails under set -e, setup aborts before the resolve, and no lock check runs for that repo."},
  {"file": "tools/kotlin/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/kotlin", "line": 34, "summary": "This new task uses print_yellow (lines 34, 177, 181), which helpers marks as 'Kept for the tasks that already call them'. CLAUDE.md lists the status printers as print_wait, print_success, print_info, print_warn and print_error.", "failure_scenario": "Cost: new code takes up a legacy printer instead of print_info or print_warn, which spreads a helper meant to go away. It breaks the repo CLAUDE.md rule 'Status lines (`print_wait`, `print_success`, `print_info`, `print_warn`, `print_error`) go under a header or a subheader.'"}
